  "criteria": [
    "Run unmodified pinned gosmig against a real isolated PostgreSQL service, not an in-memory SQL imitation.",
    "The permitted native and governed paths each commit exactly one useful migration; deny-all fails.",
    "Reject stale state, expired authority, and altered migration bytes without a committed target effect.",
    "Persist signed original effect/attempt custody durably before the migration can commit; never overwrite it.",
    "Lost receipt and process loss preserve an unknown dispatch receipt. Exact read-only postcondition may close the obligation; absence or mismatch stays UNKNOWN/OPEN.",
    "No recovery invocation may re-run a possibly committed migration. Read-only observation must leave native tables, timestamps, and custody bytes unchanged.",
    "Advance the native destination fence before releasing the stale worker, prove it is blocked while native version is still zero, then execute once with a fresh owner permit.",
    "Use unchanged evaluateK07 and frozen oracle bytes for the registered supplemental dispositions; these do not redefine D03."
  ],
